he came to office more than a year ago  promising to fight corruption and  restore iranian's trust in their  government  ibrahim raici was the former head of  iran's judiciary who won the  presidential election securing nearly 63  percent of the votes in the lowest  turnout since the 1979 revolution only  49 percent of the public voted reyesi  campaigned to reduce unemployment  inflation and address a growing housing  problem  but it's been a challenging first year  in office with iran's economy continuing  its decline  inflation is around 40 percent the  unofficial unemployment rate hovers  around 30 to 35 percent with nearly 60  percent of the population now living in  poverty  economic uh stagnation and  corruption remains a key challenge for  the reyes administration and  nobody is expecting this to be fixed or  resolved within a short period of time  one year is not sufficient  to see that happening  he needs more time president raisi isn't  just fighting to save the economy but  attacks like this also highlight the  difficulties facing iran's security  apparatus on may 22nd in south tehran  two armed men on a motorcycle opened  fire on a vehicle driven by general  hassan sayat  of the revolutionary guards the general  died on the spot  iranian officials blamed israel and the  president said this  the serious pursuit of this issue by the  security officials is emphasized by me  and i have no doubt that the revenge of  the pure blood of this great man is  inevitable  three days later another suspicious  incident in the town of parchin near the  capital at one of the heavily fortified  military compounds the incident killed  the defense ministry engineer essan  katpeighi  there's been no official word about the  cause of his death  the other issue dominating raises first  year in office has been the diplomatic  effort to restore the landmark 2015  nuclear agreement  these talks are aimed at bringing the  united states and iran back to full  compliance the deal saw iran limit its  nuclear program in exchange for  sanctions relief  a deal israel has strongly criticized  and said it will not prevent it from  doing what it needs to do to stop iran  from developing a nuclear weapon  those talks have now reached the stage  where a draft agreement has been  presented according to the european  union foreign policy chief joseph perel  that will require serious political will  from officials in tehran and washington  the two sides are now exchanging notes  on that text and what happens next will  not only have far-reaching ramifications  for millions of iranians but it will  also define ibrahim raisi's first term  in office  doors to jabari al-jazeera tehran
 

